/C [ 0 0 0 ] /Contents (0:00\2051:00\012\012Imagine a friend sends a cropped screenshot saying city buses will be free next month. This example is fictional. You want to help friends with transport costs, so you are tempted to forward it. What would you check first? The screenshot has no date and no original announcement. Digital Citizen Reflection helps us describe that habit, compare relevant evidence, and choose a realistic change. Today I will show the four steps, then you can reflect privately. You can use a fictional example throughout.\012\012Presenter cue: Pause for the opening question. Do not ask for personal disclosures.\012\012) /QuadPoints [ 1234 12 1254 12 1234 32 1254 32 ] /Rect [ 1234 12 1254 32 ] /Subtype /Text /Type /Annot
>>
endobj
