/C [ 0 0 0 ] /Contents (2:00\2053:00\012\012The same four steps work across attention, privacy, news, and AI tools. Observe means describing something you actually do, and when it happens. Evaluate means looking at a source, its date, who it covers, and its limitations. Identify means naming a risk while keeping sight of a benefit you value. Act means choosing one realistic change, a way to check what happens, and a date to review it. The page suggests a review seven days ahead, but you can change it. The aim is a useful action plan rather than a score or a judgment about the person.\012\012Presenter cue: Name each step slowly. Transition to the live page. Keep slides 4\2057 available as the screenshot backup.\012\012) /QuadPoints [ 1234 12 1254 12 1234 32 1254 32 ] /Rect [ 1234 12 1254 32 ] /Subtype /Text /Type /Annot
>>
endobj
